    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p12_b12",
      "text": "The exact promptwise solution from Section 3 tells us what a regret-robust policy should\nlook like once a prompt has been reduced to a finite simplex. RLHF training, however,\nnever gets to move probability mass on that simplex directly. What it actually sees are\nsampled completions from a language model, and what it actually updates are model\nparameters.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        310.82,
        524.95,
        394.42
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        1243,
        2099,
        1577
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.87,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 356,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p12_b13",
      "text": "Throughout this section we specialize to the \u21131 ambiguity geometry, whose locality is\nwhat makes the sampled bonus implementable; Section 4.5 and Proposition 4.5 explains\nthis choice.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        400.41,
        523.33,
        448.2
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        1601,
        2093,
        1792
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.92,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 183,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p12_b14",
      "text": "Those two viewpoints are close enough to guide the algorithm, but different enough to\ncreate real work. For a fixed prompt, the response space is astronomically large, so the\nadversarial coordinate from Proposition 3.3 is hidden from us and can only be glimpsed\nthrough a small sampled group. And even if the promptwise optimizer were available\nin closed form, it would still not produce a usable LLM update, because the policy is\nan LLM parameterized by \u03b8 and the trainable object is \u03b8, not the full vector \u03c0(\u00b7 | x).\nThe way forward is therefore to rewrite the robust objective as a policy-gradient recipe,\nunderstand what bonus the exact theory implies, and then relax that bonus until it can\nbe estimated reliably from grouped rollouts.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        454.27,
        525.55,
        609.55
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        1817,
        2102,
        2438
      ],
